How many different combinations will give T a value of true. One
of them is (A=true, B=false, C=false, D=false) . Count all of the
combinations that produce a value of true and write it in the
blank for #40. Your answer will be an integer from 1-16.
boolean A,B,C,D,T;
// A, B, C, and D are assigned some values.
T = A && !B || C && !D;

